val from your party are  two very different things and in a  I marry the goal of which would be not  to defeat Donald Trump in the primary  it's not going to happen but to do some  damage to Trump that is going to be  significantly influenced by the  difference between Republicans approving  of Trump 79 percent versus 95 percent so  that's important also important there  are three areas where Republicans  actually disapprove of Trump's handling  more than they disapprove of him overall  so again remember 79 percent of  Republicans approve of Trump  however only 77 percent think he's  handling health care correctly only 75  percent say he's handling foreign policy  correctly and only 70 percent believe  he's handling gun policy correctly this  is important and it's interesting but  Republicans are not going to vote for a  Democrat because they disagree with  Trump on these issues this is important  to understand for Democrats gun policy  isn't a voting issue by and large for  Republicans gun policy can be a voting  issue if you are on the wrong side of  more guns in more places but the reality  is if you're a Republican and you don't  love Trump's take on guns you're not  gonna go and vote for a Democrat over  that that's the reality  Healthcare a lot of these Republicans  25% of them they might recognize Trump  is completely bungling healthcare but  they're not going to go and vote for a  so-called socialist health care plan  from a Democrat they're still gonna vote  Trump they just don't like what he's  doing on health care  similarly foreign policy foreign policy  is just not a voting issue in the way  that domestic economic issues are so  that gets us to what do we do with this  data whether it's 36 percent approval or  32 percent approval or even in the  twenties Donald Trump can still win  reelection  I've I've run the numbers before with  you half the country doesn't vote you  could have a 26 percent approval and  turnout 1% more voters in some key  states than the other party and win  because half the country doesn't vote so  following Donald Trump's approval is  relevant and it helps us to understand  how people especially Republicans are  reacting to Trump it does not tell us  any  thing about what's going to happen in  2020 all you need to know is that Donald  Trump could have a 36 percent approval  rating and easily win and by the way the  fact that he has a 36 percent approval  rating tells us that there are tens of  millions of people who are so  disconnected from reality  or ideologically blinded that they don't  care what happens in the real world they  are voting for Trump in 2020 period okay  Trump has tens of millions of votes in  2020 already it's August of 2019 the  elections in November of 2020 Trump has  tens of millions of votes once you know  that you realize this becomes  get-out-the-vote because we're not going  to be able to convince these people in  any large numbers I know I'm a broken  record at this point I've been talking  about this for so long this is going to  be about get out the vote that needs to  be our priority in our context heading  into 2020 tell me if you think there is  some other way in which Trump's approval  is relevant beyond reminding us he's got  tens of millions of votes in the bank  already and we've got to get the vote  out follow us on instagram at  instagram.com slash david pakman show  and oh I have a new story on my  Instagram page David Pakman got back  from vacation big developments with my  tomato plants huge developments make  sure you're following me on instagram at  instagram.com  slash david hackman
 

